The [[Stadion Gdańsk]] in Gdańsk was selected by the UEFA Executive Committee during their meeting in [[Kyiv]] on 24 May 2018.<ref name="venue">{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaleague/news/0255-0e99f554980e-63465ec08dbc-1000--2022-uefa-europa-league-final-to-be-held-in-seville/ |title=Seville to host 2021 UEFA Europa League final |website=UEFA.com |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=24 September 2019 |access-date=28 September 2019}}</ref><ref name="el20">{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaleague/news/0245-0e98d40b6826-86b29d622244-1000--2021-uefa-europa-league-final-gdansk/ |title=Gdansk to host 2020 UEFA Europa League final |website=UEFA.com |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=24 May 2018 |access-date=28 September 2019}}</ref>

On 17 June 2020, the UEFA Executive Committee announced that due to the postponement and relocation of the [[2020 UEFA Europa League final|2020 final]], Gdańsk would instead host the 2021 final.<ref name="Exco17June"/>

==Background==
This was Villarreal's fourth ever final in an official [[Tournament#Knockout tournaments|knockout tournament]], having played previously three in [[UEFA competitions]], all in the [[UEFA Intertoto Cup]], winning it in [[2003 UEFA Intertoto Cup|2003]] and [[2004 UEFA Intertoto Cup|2004]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/mediaservices/informationkits/ |title=UEFA Super Cup - 2021 season |type=Press Kit |website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=11 August 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Tejedor Carnicero |first=José Vicente |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tabless/spancuphist.html |title=Spain – List of Cup Finals |work=[[RSSSF]] |date=22 April 2021 |access-date=6 May 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Torre |first=Raúl |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tabless/spanleagcuphist.html |title=Spain – List of League Cup Finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |date=29 January 2009 |access-date=6 May 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Tejedor Carnicero |first1=José Vicente |last2=Torre |first2=Raúl |last3=Lozano Ferrer |first3=Carles |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tabless/spansupcuphist.html |title=Spain – List of Super Cup Finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |date=28 January 2021 |access-date=6 May 2021}}</ref> On the other hand, this was head coach [[Unai Emery]]'s fifth European final, all in the UEFA Europa League; he won three successive titles with [[Sevilla FC|Sevilla]] in [[2014 UEFA Europa League final|2014]], [[2015 UEFA Europa League final|2015]] and [[2016 UEFA Europa League final|2016]], before losing in [[2019 UEFA Europa League final|2019]] with [[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/printoutfiles/competitions/uefaeuropaleague/2021/e/e_2029909_pk.pdf|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210526073132/https://www.uefa.com/printoutfiles/competitions/uefaeuropaleague/2021/e/e_2029909_pk.pdf|url-status=dead|archive-date=26 May 2021|title=2021 UEFA Europa League Final|type=Press Kit|date=26 May 2021|website=UEFA.com |publisher=Union of European Football Associations|accessdate= 26 May 2021}}</ref>

This was Manchester United's second UEFA Cup/Europa League final, having won the only previous occasion in [[2017 UEFA Europa League final|2017]]. Overall, it was their eighth European major final between the European Cup/Champions League, Cup Winners' Cup, and the UEFA Cup/Europa League. [[Ole Gunnar Solskjær]] reached his first final as the club's manager, having scored the winning goal in the [[1999 UEFA Champions League final]] playing for them, exactly 22 years prior.<ref>{{cite news |first=Simon |last=Stone |title=Roma 3-2 Man Utd (5-8 on aggregate): Solskjaer's side through to Europa League final |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/57000593|work=BBC Sport |date=6 May 2021 |access-date=6 May 2021 }}</ref>

The clubs previously met four times, in the [[2005–06 UEFA Champions League group stage#Group D|2005–06]] and [[2008–09 UEFA Champions League group stage#Group E|2008–09]] UEFA Champions League group stages. All games ended in goalless draws.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.worldfootball.net/teams/te2102/villarreal-cf/records-all-time-appearances/ |title=Villarreal CF » Record against Manchester United |website=WorldFootball.net |access-date=6 May 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Manchester United football club: record v Villarreal |url=https://www.11v11.com/teams/manchester-united/tab/opposingTeams/opposition/Villarreal/ |website=11v11.com |access-date=6 May 2021}}</ref>

